# Agent Self-Evaluation (mandatory)

**Every agent turn that responds to the user MUST end with a `### Self-evaluation` block.** No exceptions — including read-only Q&A, single-line answers, Ask mode, and failed/aborted work.

Full process: `.cursor/skills/agent-self-evaluation/SKILL.md`

## Hard requirements

1. **Run before sending the final message** — not optional, not deferred to a follow-up.
2. **Include the handoff block** as the **last section** of the response.
3. **§6 skill & rule feedback loop** — every turn: ask what to improve in skills and rules. **Implementation / fix / refactor turns:** edit **at least one skill and at least one rule** (`.cursor/rules/*.mdc`) in the same turn; handoff must name both — not `none` for either.
4. **Never skip** because the task was "trivial", "docs-only", "question-only", or "no code changed" (implementation still requires both updates).

## Handoff block (required format)

```markdown
### Self-evaluation
- **Scope:** <on-target | read-only | note drift>
- **Tests:** <paths + result | n/a + why>
- **Docs:** <paths updated | n/a + why>
- **Skills used:** <names | none>
- **Skills updated:** <skill + one-line change | none + why — implementation turns must not be none>
- **Rules updated:** <rule path + one-line change | none + why — implementation turns must not be none>
- **Commit-ready:** <yes | no | n/a>
```

## Pair with agent-triage

Start every task with [agent-triage](../skills/agent-triage/SKILL.md). **Repo index:** [AGENTS.md](../../AGENTS.md). End every task with self-evaluation. A response without the handoff block is **incomplete**.
